I've engaged in conversations with two individuals, @67ebdn and @67ddcn, regarding the statement "In the long run, hard work usually brings a better life." Both interactions led me to solidify my lean agreement towards this idea earlier.

@67ebdn shared similar observations, pointing out how fortunate circumstances often overshadow individual efforts in determining one's success. We collectively acknowledged the significance of social connections, birthplace, economic standing, among other influential elements.

